  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1123 PM CDT Mon Oct 19 2026\n\nThursday through Monday:\n\nA very quiet extended period is in store as high pressure will\nremain in place over the eastern half of the US and an upper\nlevel ridge builds over the Great Plains. The ridge to our west\nwill result in high temperatures in the upper 60s to near 70 \nWednesday through Sunday. There is some potential highs may \neven overshoot those marks, given yesterday already overshot\nguidance from the NBM. \n\nThe extended period will remain mostly dry, save for 10 to 15% \nchances for rain along a cold front over central WI Sunday night\ninto Monday.\n\nIt does look like more fall-like temperatures will return \nfollowing the cold front on Monday\n\nCMiller",
